<component type="desktop-application">
	<id>ca.liminalhq.mailslot</id>
	<launchable type="desktop-id">ca.liminalhq.mailslot.desktop</launchable>

	<name>Mailslot</name>
	<summary>A private drop slot for files sent your way</summary>
	<developer id="ca.liminalhq">
		<name>Liminal HQ</name>
	</developer>

	<metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
	<project_license>Apache-2.0 OR MIT</project_license>

	<description>
		<p>Mailslot receives files through a private link. Start sharing, hand out the link, and files sent to it land in a folder on your computer with a SHA-256 checksum. Nothing is ever served back.</p>
		<p>It also sends. The same app and its command-line companion push files to another Mailslot, resume interrupted transfers and skip files the other side already has.</p>
		<p>Features:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>A web upload page that works on phones, plus curl and Mailslot clients</li>
			<li>QR code and mailslot:// links for quick pairing</li>
			<li>Resumable uploads and duplicate detection</li>
			<li>Link expiry, size and quota limits, bad-token lockout and optional HTTPS</li>
			<li>Optional UPnP port mapping that is time-limited and clearly shown</li>
			<li>A Send page with a queue that survives restarts</li>
		</ul>
	</description>

